text:
The plate is a square dinner plate, roughly 26 cm across. It holds two corn cob pieces, each about 5 cm across and 3-4 cm long, so each is a short cross-cut section. A section like that weighs about 50-60 g of kernels plus cob, which makes roughly 110 g for both.

Corn on the cob runs about 90-100 kcal per 100 g including the cob. Counting only the edible kernels, the two pieces come to about 60-70 g, or around 100 kcal. The cob adds mass but little energy, so I estimate about 100 kcal and 120 g total.

